{
  "$description": "Protect Line app layer (GUI2-03): semantic UI tokens with light and dark sets, status colours, compact type and density, and the data-viz palette. Builds on tokens/foundation.tokens.json — aliases like {color.navy} resolve across both files. scripts/build-tokens.js turns this file into app-tokens.css, tokens/tailwind.css and tokens/app.resolved.json; --check fails if any of them is stale. CSS name rule: \"--\" + path joined with \"-\", a trailing \"default\" segment dropped, and the \"theme.light.\" / \"theme.dark.\" prefix removed.",
  "color": {
    "dark-blue": {
      "450": {
        "$type": "color",
        "$value": { "colorSpace": "srgb", "components": [0.3686, 0.349, 0.6118], "hex": "#5e599c" },
        "$description": "App layer addition (GUI2-03), not in the Figma foundations — needs brand approval. Subtle text ink. Sits halfway between dark-blue-400 and -500 on the same hue (OKLCH h≈285). dark-blue-400 is only 4.49:1 on fair blue and 4.15:1 on dark-blue-100, so it cannot carry captions on a selected row; this step is 6.2:1 on white and ≥5.07:1 on every light app surface."
      }
    },
    "pink": {
      "950": {
        "$type": "color",
        "$value": { "colorSpace": "srgb", "components": [0.2627, 0.102, 0.302], "hex": "#431a4d" },
        "$description": "App layer addition (GUI2-03), not in the Figma foundations — needs brand approval. Dark-mode tint for the attention status (pink-600 mixed 30% into navy in OKLab). Keeps mid-pink text at 5.09:1. The Figma pink ramp stops at 900, which is too bright and red to sit behind text on navy."
      }
    },
